{
 "description": "Configuration of the OGD monitor, shared by scripts/monitor/ogd_monitor.py and src/components/OgdMonitor. One entry per monitored product. metric 'age': minutes since the collection's newest item was updated; metric 'latency': publication latency in minutes, i.e. time from the data's reference time (timestamp in the file name, or newest reference_timestamp in a *_now.csv) to its availability (asset creation on the STAC API, or the file's Last-Modified). ok_max_min: up to this counts as up to date; warn_max_min: up to this counts as delayed, beyond as down. For latency entries, a product also counts as down when its newest reference time is older than interval_min + warn_max_min (no new data). null thresholds = static, not monitored. realtime: counts towards OKR O3-KR1. The order of items is the display order (as in the documentation); sub: true marks a single station shown under its collection. doc: path of the documentation page (without locale); null = title without link. monitoring_pending: true shows 'monitoring to follow' instead of the history strip. source.complete_run: true measures latency until the last file of a model run is available (all parameters), not the first.",
 "stac_api": "https://data.geo.admin.ch/api/stac/v1",
